{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBQpzmHdijRmSowGTJLb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 13 (Sb 0.589 / Zn 0.411). Its EQE was 0.0858%, the highest of the three compositions I measured. There's a real chance something more Zn-rich is better, because EQE was still rising at the last point measured.\n\nI used all 3 merit measurements and 3 of the 5 XRD measurements:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 22 | 0.804 | 0.0673 |\n| 16 | 0.678 | 0.0701 |\n| 13 | 0.589 | **0.0858** |\n\n- **Where I started:** Zn:Sb = 1:2 is the ratio of ZnSb₂O₆, a known photoanode oxide. So I took the first reading near that point (index 16) and a second on the Sb-rich side (index 22).\n- **XRD:** films at Sb 0.56, 0.68 and 0.77 all showed the same main pattern, which I read as the ZnSb₂O₆ structure. A second set of peaks got stronger as Sb went up, which suggests an extra phase in the Sb-rich films.\n- **Result:** EQE went up steadily as the films got more Zn-rich. The trend was still climbing at index 13, so the true peak may be further toward Zn (roughly Sb 0.45–0.56, indices 9–12). No merit budget was left to check. I didn't measure anything below Sb 0.56 at all, not even by XRD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":7987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437},"output_tokens":487,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56f68aa8-d342-47b0-888b-48f6a13ee269","uuid":"04f723f3-4a47-452c-9d6f-c6d78ea07ed9","timestamp":"2026-09-18T18:53:55.844Z","request_id":"req_011CfBQpzH1oorHexaAkHxFJ"}
